<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suddhodana</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Śuddhodana</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suddhodana was a chief of the Shakya clan and the father of Siddhartha Gautama, the Buddha. Early texts describe him as a leader of the Shakya assembly at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kapilavastu">Kapilavastu</a>, while later tradition made him a king. His wife Maya died soon after the Buddha's birth, and her sister Mahapajapati raised the child.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suddhodana.jpg" alt="Suddhodana" width="320" height="454" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Nomu420 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suddhodna_seated_on_a_throne_Roundel_2_ivory_tusk.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
